 To find the orthogonal projection of $9e_1$ onto the subspace spanned by $[2, 2, 1, 0]$ and $[-2, 2, 0, 1]$, we need to solve the equation $A^T A \mathbf{x} = A^T \mathbf{v}$, where $A$ is the matrix formed by the spanning vectors and $\mathbf{v} = 9e_1 = [9, 0, 0, 0]^T$. The matrix $A$ is:
$$
A = \begin{bmatrix}
2 & -2 \\
2 & 2 \\
1 & 0 \\
0 & 1
\end{bmatrix}
$$
Then $A^T A$ is:
$$
A^T A = \begin{bmatrix}
2 & 2 & 1 & 0 \\
-2 & 2 & 0 & 1
\end{bmatrix}
\begin{bmatrix}
2 & -2 \\
2 & 2 \\
1 & 0 \\
0 & 1
\end{bmatrix}
= \begin{bmatrix}
9 & 0 \\
0 & 9
\end{bmatrix}
$$
And $A^T \mathbf{v}$ is:
$$
A^T \mathbf{v} = \begin{bmatrix}
2 & 2 & 1 & 0 \\
-2 & 2 & 0 & 1
\end{bmatrix}
\begin{bmatrix}
9 \\
0 \\
0 \\
0
\end{bmatrix}
= \begin{bmatrix}
18 \\
-18
\end{bmatrix}
$$
Solving $A^T A \mathbf{x} = A^T \mathbf{v}$, we get:
$$
\begin{bmatrix}
9 & 0 \\
0 & 9
\end{bmatrix}
\begin{bmatrix}
x_1 \\
x_2
\end{bmatrix}
=
\begin{bmatrix}
18 \\
-18
\end{bmatrix}
\Rightarrow
\begin{bmatrix}
x_1 \\
x_2
\end{bmatrix}
=
\begin{bmatrix}
2 \\
-2
\end{bmatrix}
$$
The projection vector is $A \mathbf{x}$:
$$
A \begin{bmatrix}
2 \\
-2
\end{bmatrix}
=
\begin{bmatrix}
2 & -2 \\
2 & 2 \\
1 & 0 \\
0 & 1
\end{bmatrix}
\begin{bmatrix}
2 \\
-2
\end{bmatrix}
=
\begin{bmatrix}
0 \\
0 \\
2 \\
-2
\end{bmatrix}
$$
The answer is (D).
